  "body": "I'm pretty new to synapse setup, but I guess documentation is mainly for inexperienced users.\r\n\r\nImo documentation https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/master/docs/metrics-howto.md about setting up metrics running locally is quite confusing as it suggests adding second listener, but then my server did not federate at all. After help in synapse room I finally made it work properly with config below for synapse 1.33\r\n\r\n```\r\nlisteners:\r\n  - port: 8008\r\n    tls: false\r\n    type: http\r\n    x_forwarded: true\r\n    bind_addresses: ['127.0.0.1']\r\n\r\n    resources:\r\n      - names: [client, federation]\r\n        compress: false\r\n\r\n  - port: 9000\r\n    tls: false\r\n    type: http\r\n    x_forwarded: false\r\n    bind_addresses: ['127.0.0.1']\r\n\r\n    resources:\r\n    - names: [metrics]\r\n      compress: false\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\nI suggest similar example is added to doc (of course polished to best practice) or at least mentioned not adding new listener section or adjusted so second listener actually works.",
